            0.26,
            0.881,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "(i) What is a suitable representation of this data — a stacked bar chart or a 100% stacked bar chart? Why do you think so?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.191,
            0.299,
            0.881,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Suppose a 100% stacked bar chart is drawn. Which of the following question(s) can be answered by looking at just that chart?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.356,
            0.593,
            0.375
          ],
          "content": "(a) Who finished the race first?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.241,
            0.376,
            0.881,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": "(b) Approximately what fraction of their race time did Athlete 1 spend cycling?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.245,
            0.413,
            0.765,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "(c) Which athlete took the longest for running?"
